Priority: P0
Title:    [P0] Remediate /opt/cpanel/ea-php74/root/usr/sbin/php-fpm (LIKELY_VULNERABLE, SAPI: fpm)
Steps:
  1. Branch 7.4 has no verified upstream fix (EOL/unfixed); major-version migration, needs application testing (target: 8.5 (>= 8.5.12)). Check for vendor or LTS backports, and keep configuration mitigations as a stop-gap.
  2. Temporary configuration mitigation (applies to CVE-2026-109619 only; not a fix):
     Create drop-in INI file /etc/php/conf.d/99-mitigation.ini:
       session.upload_progress.enabled = 0
     Alternatively, in FPM pool config (/usr/local/etc/php-fpm.d/www.conf):
       php_admin_value[session.upload_progress.enabled] = 0
Commands:
  [Vendor update tooling (cPanel / CloudLinux)] use your vendor's update tooling
Restart Hints:
  - reload php-fpm (e.g. systemctl reload php-fpm)
Notes:    WARNING: A configuration mitigation is a temporary risk reduction only and is NOT a fix. CVE-2026-109618 has no known configuration mitigation; upgrading PHP is required.
